{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Social Interaction — Affect Convergence and Support Exchange\"\n",
        "format: html\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## What This Code Does\n",
        "\n",
        "This demo exercises the core dyadic interaction function `process_interaction()` directly (not via the `run_phase` stub). It varies partner affect [−1, 1] and self affect [−1, 1] across all five stress state scenarios, observing affect/resilience convergence, resource exchange, and support detection.\n",
        "\n",
        "The theory predicts: negativity bias (negative influences amplified 1.5×), convergence dynamics (affect and resilience move toward each other mediated by influence_rate), support detection when convergence magnitude exceeds a threshold, and five state-machine scenarios (win-win, lose-lose, self-helped, self-harmed, mutual-growth).\n",
        "\n",
        "## Setup"
      ],
      "id": "97ed0964"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: setup\n",
        "import os\n",
        "import sys\n",
        "import pathlib\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "from numpy.random import Generator, PCG64\n",
        "\n",
        "demos_dir = pathlib.Path(os.getcwd())\n",
        "project_root = demos_dir.parents[2]\n",
        "sys.path.insert(0, str(project_root))\n",
        "\n",
        "from src.python.phases.interaction import process_interaction"
      ],
      "id": "setup",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Step 1: Sweep Partner and Self Affect\n",
        "\n",
        "We vary partner affect [−1, 1] and self affect [−1, 1] across three stress-state combinations."
      ],
      "id": "e1e79eca"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: sweep\n",
        "N_PARTNER_A, N_SELF_A = 20, 5\n",
        "rng = Generator(PCG64(42))\n",
        "records = []\n",
        "\n",
        "stress_combos = [\n",
        "    (False, False), (True, False), (True, True),\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "for self_stressed, partner_stressed in stress_combos:\n",
        "    for partner_affect in np.linspace(-1, 1, N_PARTNER_A):\n",
        "        for self_affect in np.linspace(-1, 1, N_SELF_A):\n",
        "            self_state = {\"affect\": self_affect, \"resilience\": 0.5, \"stressed\": self_stressed}\n",
        "            partner_state = {\"affect\": partner_affect, \"resilience\": 0.5, \"stressed\": partner_stressed}\n",
        "            config = {\"influence_rate\": 0.05, \"resilience_influence\": 0.05,\n",
        "                      \"support_threshold\": 0.02, \"boost\": 0.10, \"cost\": 0.05, \"small_boost\": 0.02}\n",
        "            self_out, partner_out = process_interaction(self_state, partner_state, config, rng)\n",
        "            records.append({\n",
        "                \"self_affect\": self_affect, \"partner_affect\": partner_affect,\n",
        "                \"self_stressed\": int(self_stressed), \"partner_stressed\": int(partner_stressed),\n",
        "                \"self_affect_change\": self_out[\"state_delta\"].get(\"affect\", 0),\n",
        "                \"partner_affect_change\": partner_out[\"state_delta\"].get(\"affect\", 0),\n",
        "                \"self_resilience_change\": self_out[\"state_delta\"].get(\"resilience\", 0),\n",
        "                \"partner_resilience_change\": partner_out[\"state_delta\"].get(\"resilience\", 0),\n",
        "                \"self_resource_change\": self_out[\"state_delta\"].get(\"resources\", 0),\n",
        "                \"partner_resource_change\": partner_out[\"state_delta\"].get(\"resources\", 0),\n",
        "                \"support_occurred\": int(self_out[\"observation\"][\"support_occurred\"]),\n",
        "            })\n",
        "\n",
        "df = pd.DataFrame(records)\n",
        "print(f\"Generated {len(df)} interaction records\")"
      ],
      "id": "sweep",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Step 2: Correlogram — Interaction Variables\n",
        "\n",
        "The 8×8 PairGrid is coloured by whether support was exchanged (orange = support, grey = no support)."
      ],
      "id": "0669997e"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: fig-correlogram\n",
        "vars_ = [\"self_affect\", \"partner_affect\", \"self_affect_change\", \"partner_affect_change\",\n",
        "         \"self_resilience_change\", \"partner_resilience_change\",\n",
        "         \"self_resource_change\", \"partner_resource_change\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "g = sns.PairGrid(df, vars=vars_, hue=\"support_occurred\",\n",
        "                 palette={0: \"#bdc3c7\", 1: \"#e67e22\"}, diag_sharey=False)\n",
        "g.map_upper(sns.scatterplot, s=4, alpha=0.4)\n",
        "g.map_lower(sns.scatterplot, s=4, alpha=0.4)\n",
        "g.map_diag(sns.kdeplot, fill=True)\n",
        "g.add_legend(title=\"Support\", bbox_to_anchor=(1.05, 0.5), loc=\"center left\")\n",
        "plt.suptitle(\"Interaction — Affect Convergence and Resource Exchange\", y=1.02, fontsize=13)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "fig-correlogram",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## What We See\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Negativity bias**: negative partner/self affect produces disproportionately large affect change (1.5×), visible as asymmetry in change variables.\n",
        "- **Support detection**: support (orange) occurs when convergence magnitude is high — typically when affect values differ substantially.\n",
        "- **Resource exchange**: both-stressed + support → boost (win-win). Both-stressed without support → cost (lose-lose).\n",
        "- **Mutual growth**: neither stressed → small PF boost, no resource change.\n",
        "- **Affect convergence**: self and partner affect changes are opposite-signed — each moves toward the other's affect value.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Why This Matters for the Simulation\n",
        "\n",
        "Social interaction is the mechanism through which agents influence each other's emotional states and resource levels. Negativity bias amplifies the spread of negative affect through the network, which can drive cascading stress across the population. Support exchange provides a counterbalancing positive force, enabling stressed agents to receive help from better-off peers. These dynamics are central to emergent network-level phenomena."
      ],
      "id": "f023f8c2"
    }
  ],
